{"kind": "paragraph", "text": "Table 3a Probabilities of specified energy consumption obtained from Algorithm (1). The algorithm iterates a while loop for the desired peak hours duration (line 2). In each iteration, the algorithm computes for each appliance (line 3) and its corresponding thresholds (i.e.) in a given environment (line 4). Afterwards, it computes the overall load of appliances in on-state at time (line 5) along with the userstate based on the computed load (line 6). Then, the algorithm passes the user-states to Algorithm 1 that returns (line 7), which is used to get average probability of consuming maximum power in remaining peak load hours. Next, appliances in on-state are selected (line 8). For each selected appliance (line 9), the algorithm first obtains the userdefined on-off threshold for the appliance (line 10). The subsequent steps (lines 11 to line 13), are executed for these appliances if the user defined threshold is greater than the threshold of human comfort for the appliance. Therein, it computes the difference (denoted by) between the user-defined threshold () and minimum threshold required for human comfort () (line 12). The threshold value is updated based on this difference () (line 13). Algorithm 2: PF-PEC Algorithm Input: Human comfort constraints and parameters,; peak hours duration Output:,, 1: ← 0 2: while ∈ do 3: Compute for all type of loads 4: Compute for all type of loads 5: Compute load in on-state at 6: Find user state from computed load 7: Invoke Algorithm 1 and save value of 8: ← Appliances in on-state at 9: for each appliance in do 10: Obtain user defined on-off thresholds () of the appliance 11: if > then; 12: = - 13: = + × 14: end if 15: end for 16: + + 17: end while 18: return", "category": "supplementary", "reason": "definition_block", "level": 2, "section_path": ["PF-PEC algorithm operations"], "source_tag": "p", "source_type": "", "coords": "6,37.59,55.79,26.65,5.99;6,37.59,64.38,219.64,5.94;6,120.85,75.14,34.69,5.